    "created_at": "2024-11-11T12:29:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-11-11T12:30:43Z",
    "body": "> This is not something color pickers tend to support.\r\n\r\nOn the contrary, if you ignore the standard Windows/macOS color pickers and look at professional tooling like in Photoshop and Illustrator, the pickers will have a \"No color\" option that's visible when relevant (e.g. when using the Shape tool in PS, where Fills and Stroke colors are both optional): when selected, this No-color option is denoted by a red strike-through on a white background (though I'd personally prefer the transparency-grid).\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2ea0ef44-e753-4266-8932-aca96bbf06cf)\r\n\r\n",
